			"offsets": {
				"from": 0,
				"to": 15740
			},
			"text": " Hi, it's quantum computer news time. The Microsoft CEO just dropped this. A couple of reflections on the quantum computing breakthrough we just announced. Most of us grew up learning there are three main types of matter, solar, liquid and gas. Today, that changed."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:15,740",
				"to": "00:00:30,380"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 15740,
				"to": 30380
			},
			"text": " So, after a 20-year pursuit, awesome, we've been working on it a long time, we've created an entirely new state of matter, unlocked by a new class of materials, topoconductors, that enable a fundamental leap in computing."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:30,380",
				"to": "00:00:45,700"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 30380,
				"to": 45700
			},
			"text": " It powers the Majorana 1, I believe that's how it's pronounced, the first quantum processing unit built on a topological core. We believe this breakthrough will allow us to create a truly meaningful quantum computer, not in decades as some have predicted, but in years."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:45,740",
				"to": "00:01:02,320"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 45740,
				"to": 62320
			},
			"text": " Now, of course, that's the problem with quantum computers, and I'll link in my quantum computer videos down here with Professor Andrea Morello from the University of New South Wales, who's one of the world's leading quantum computer researchers, and I've got some great videos down there, so check those out."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:02,320",
				"to": "00:01:15,700"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 62320,
				"to": 75700
			},
			"text": " But basically, he argues that there's no real, at the moment, there's no real practical, you know, real world use for quantum computers. They're more like, you know, obscure research type stuff."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:15,740",
				"to": "00:01:25,360"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 75740,
				"to": 85360
			},
			"text": " And things like that. Sure, in the future, that's almost certainly going to change, but at the moment, they're, you know, just toys for quantum computer people to play around with."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:25,360",
				"to": "00:01:36,320"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 85360,
				"to": 96320
			},
			"text": " The qubits created with topoconductors are faster, more reliable, and smaller. They are one one-hundredth of a millimeter, meaning we now have a clear path to a million qubit processor."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:36,620",
				"to": "00:01:45,720"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 96620,
				"to": 105720
			},
			"text": " And if you hear the rumors about quantum computers, they say, oh, with a few hundred qubits, we can, you know, break the Bitcoin algorithm, and, you know, it's all good."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:45,740",
				"to": "00:01:51,980"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 105740,
				"to": 111980
			},
			"text": " So, imagine what you could do with a million qubits. Do we have to worry about that at the moment?"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:52,100",
				"to": "00:01:57,780"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 112100,
				"to": 117780
			},
			"text": " Well, anyway, they've got some funky photos, and I've got more than this. We're going to the high-res photos of this thing."
